1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[Ikalgo] All I know is this,

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
you looked at a good-for-nothing
octopus like me,

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
and you said I was cool.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
You even said
we could have been friends.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
I can't stand by while you die!

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
I'm gonna save you!
Don't you die on me!

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
[opening theme music playing]

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
[singer singing in English]

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

10
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
POWER X AND X GAMES

11
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
[narrator] While Killua
was in the process

12
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Gon was forming a bond as well,

13
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
with a Chimera Ant
who goes by the name Meleoron.

14
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
-[Meleoron] huh?
-The smoke will stick to your clothes,

15
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
and people
will smell you coming,

16
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
but honestly,
it doesn't really matter much.

17
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
While my invisibility
is sort of like my trademark,

18
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
my real ability
goes one step further.

19
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
What?

20
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Here. I'll show you.

21
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
[inhales]

22
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
I can't sense him at all,

23
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
only the smell of cigarettes.

24
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
He's not here.

25
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
This is more than just invisibility.

26
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
without even making a sound?

27
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
That's impossible.
So how did he do it?

28
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
[gasps] Whoa!

29
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Where did you come from?

30
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Your mind simply refused
to acknowledge

31
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
It's like that, but more extreme.

32
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Turning invisible really is just a decoy.

33
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:14,000
It helps me keep my true ability
a secret from everyone else.

34
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
[Gon]
Why tell me something so important?

35
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
[Meleoron]
Well, I've gotta earn your trust, don't I?

36
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Yeah, it's kind of a risk,
but it's one I have to take.

37
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
See, if I can't get you to trust me,

38
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
then we won't be able to start anything.

39
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Huh?

40
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Like I said before,

41
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
we have to trust each other first.

42
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Once you've agreed
to be my partner,

43
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
I'll be happy to tell you
everything you want to know.

44
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
What about your buddy?

45
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Isn't he gonna have a fit
when he finds out

46
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
you teamed up
with a suspicious-looking monster?

47
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
[groans]

48
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Why the hell am I
trashing myself like this?

49
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
It's not like I chose to be this way.

50
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
He sure is restless.

51
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
[Meleoron sighs]

52
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
I guess it doesn't matter.

53
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Even a good friend
you've had for 20 years

54
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
could still stab you in the back.

55
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Time is not a matter of trust.

56
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,000
You feel me?

57
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
[groans]

58
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
This deal is dead in the water.

59
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Nah. It's fine.

60
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
I'll just insist on having it my way.

61
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
take down the King.

62
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,000
I'm taking revenge.

63
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[Gon] Hmm.

64
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
[Meleoron sighs]

65
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
If you insist,
I guess I'll have to tell you.

66
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
What? Already?

67
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,000
[lighter flicks]

68
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[gasps]

69
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
But at the time,
I didn't even realize

70
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
that someone who was
close to me had died.

71
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Huh? Why not?

72
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
You just said you saw it happen.

73
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Because I'd forgotten
who Peggy was to me.

74
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,000
I'd forgotten that he
was my foster father.

75
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
[dramatic music playing]

76
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Memories of my human days
came flooding back.

77
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
my parents' names
and my own name,

78
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
bits of my childhood.

79
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
always carrying thick books
with him everywhere.

80
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
[Gon] Then, I think I get it now.

81
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
[Meleoron] Huh?

82
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:56,000
I think I'm finally starting to understand
why I felt I could trust you so quickly.

83
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
It's 'cause you seem so human,

84
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:09,000
Really? When I met you,
I had exactly the opposite reaction.

85
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[Gon] Huh?

86
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
I could immediately sense

87
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
an inhuman beast
lurking deep within you.

88
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
That's why I wanted
to team up with you,

89
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
because we're not all
that different, you and I.

90
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
All right.
Let's get right to it, then.

91
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Oh, right. I'm Gon Freecss.

92
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:40,000
I actually have one more ability,

93
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
and we just met
the condition to activate it.

94
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[Gon gasps]

95
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Time to show you my third ability.

96
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[dramatic music playing]

97
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Ha.

98
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[bird chirping]

99
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Wait a second.

100
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Does that mean I was using
your Perfect Plan, too?

101
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
That's exactly right,

102
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:45,000
and the name of my third power
is God's Accomplice.

103
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Now do you understand
how powerful this is?

104
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
This ability will allow us
to approach and attack

105
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
No matter how powerful
the King is,

106
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:14,000
one mega-punch to his
unguarded vitals, and he's done.

107
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[Gon shudders]

108
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
[Meleoron] Hey, Gon,

109
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
you're just the perfect partner
I've been looking for.

110
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
If we work together,

111
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:29,000
we can deal that son of a bitch
an unprecedented blow.

112
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
back when you used
that Jan-Ken-Rock thing.

113
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
-Those were my men, you know.
-[gasps]

114
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,000
They're not my soldiers
or my allies anymore.

115
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Well, I guess from their perspective,
I'm the one who changed, not them.

116
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
You know someone who'd be better?

117
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
[Gon] I sure do.

118
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
I'll contact him.

119
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Hold on.

120
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Right or wrong, I do trust you.

121
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
And I won't even regret my decision,

122
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
because I watched you,
and I spoke to you,

123
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,000
just because you trust them.

124
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
That's not how this is gonna work.

125
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
That make sense to you?

126
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Mm-hmm. I get your point, but still--

127
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Hey, it's my life
on the line here, right?

128
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Listen. My Perfect Plan's
not invincible at all.

129
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
It's actually more vulnerable
than you might think.

130
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,000
as somebody with my ability,
what would they do then?

131
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Hate to say it,
but when it comes to combat,

132
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,000
I'm the weakest
Chimera Ant around.

133
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
I'm basically a foot soldier.

134
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Forget the King.

135
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
I couldn't even survive a punch
from a squadron leader.

136
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
If I just turn invisible,
I can be located with En.

137
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
It's already been tested,

138
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,000
so the other squadron leaders
know it, too.

139
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,000
I need my enemies to believe
that my power is weak.

140
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
They need to think
just a little bit of En

141
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,000
My point is that
I don't want to reveal my power

142
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
to anyone else,

143
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,000
not even if it's someone you trust.

144
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,000
You understand?

145
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
[Gon] Find out for yourself.

146
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Huh?

147
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,000
I'll call him over,
but I won't mention that you're here.

148
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
-[cell phone beeps]
-[Meleoron] Hey, wait.

149
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
-You can watch things from a distance.
-[phone line ringing]

150
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
-Hi. It's--
-[Knuckle] Hey!

151
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
I've been waiting, idiot.

152
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,000
The boss had to make a move
because of you two kids.

153
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
The original plan's
been completely derailed,

154
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
but I approve of what
you're doing out there.

155
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Uh…

156
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:55,000
[Knuckle] We can't just let five million
innocent people die like that.

157
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,000
The boss already used his ability
to surround the capital.

158
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,000
[Gon] really?

159
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
so they're not going to be able

160
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,000
to perform any kind
of long-distance sorting.

161
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
[Gon] Right.

162
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
[Knuckle] However, the boss and Mr. Knov

163
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:17,000
will be expending all their
energy to delay Neferpitou,

164
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
which means,
when the operation begins,

165
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:25,000
they're not gonna be in any condition
to take on the Royal Guards.

166
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[sighs]

167
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
We fully expect
that more citizens

168
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
will gather in the capital
for the celebration.

169
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
There might still be a massacre.

170
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
The situation
hasn't gotten any less grim.

171
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
We can't contact
the chairman anymore.

172
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
He's focusing and honing
his energy somewhere,

173
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
[dramatic music playing]

174
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
The four of us
need to make a choice.

175
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Do we summon reinforcements,

176
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
or face the three Royal Guards
all by ourselves?

177
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[Gon] He's not here.

178
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Are you saying
that you two split up?

179
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Oh, I get it.
He was doing all this himself.

180
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Can you call him?

181
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
We should all touch base real soon,

182
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
-and the sooner, the better.
-[Gon] Yeah.

183
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
We need to find
a halfway point for us

184
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
where we can meet up
when we can.

185
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
[Shoot] Mm.

186
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
[Knuckle] Here. Mandai City.

187
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Right. Got it.

188
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,000
[hangs up]

189
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,000
[King] Checkmate.

190
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
Now, why didn't you concede defeat?

191
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Uh…

192
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
[wincing]

193
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
[King] Do not make me repeat myself.

194
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
The match was decided
22 moves ago.

195
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
So then tell me
why you didn't concede.

196
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Did you actually think
that I would make a mistake?

197
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
[gasping]

198
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[yelps]

199
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
[King] The fool.

200
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[dramatic music playing]

201
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,000
[man] Please, let me go!
What do you want?

202
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Someone, anyone, help me!

203
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
[groans]

204
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
[man gasping]

205
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
[exclaims fearfully]

206
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
I'm just tired, that's all.

207
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
That's why I lost.

208
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
I might have a slight fever.

209
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
I'm really dizzy and weak.

210
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Take eight hours and medicine.

211
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
I want you in top condition.

212
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Lose again, and I won't be
interested in your excuses.

213
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
So rest like you mean it.

214
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
These games are quite difficult.

215
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
I'm shocked that it took you

216
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,000
less than half the time
it took to learn Shogi.

217
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,000
I just learned the trick to it.
That was all.

218
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
but every first-rate player
has a certain rhythm to his play.

219
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:02,000
The key is to disrupt their rhythm,
and therefore their game.

220
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,000
As soon as you learn the basics,
you can deduce their rhythm…

221
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
[dramatic music playing]

222
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:12,000
[King] …and once you know their rhythm,
disrupting it is easy.

223
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,000
A psychological approach
that would apply to any contest.

224
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
It's a board game
that they call Gungi.

225
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
and nearly all the citizens there
know how to play it.

226
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,000
However, pieces can be
stacked up to three high,

227
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
and the opening formation
of pieces is variable.

228
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,000
It requires
three-dimensional thinking,

229
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,000
making it somewhat different

230
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
from other board games
of this nature.

231
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
World tournaments have
been held around the globe

232
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
who is a five-time reigning champion.

233
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Hmm.
So then if I defeat this champion,

234
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
I'll be the best in the world?

235
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
A fitting end to this diversion.

236
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
[cane tapping]

237
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:57,000
[narrator] Six days left
until the sorting.

238
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:01,000
A young girl appears
who will shape the fate of the King.

239
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,000
But in what way, exactly,

240
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:06,000
he has no idea at all.

241
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,000
[closing theme music playing]

242
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:14,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

243
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
[upbeat music playing]

244
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, "Check and Mate."

245
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,000
-I'm Gon.
-[Killua] I'm Gillua.

246
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
-[Gon] Did you change your name?
-[Killua] What? No way.

247
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,000
[Gon] Say it again.

248
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
-[Killua] I'm Killua.
-[Gon] O.M.G.!

249
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:45,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
